From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thuong Vo <66083331+SekiroKenjii@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] foundry, lsp, podman: look up programs off the main thread

A file's first diagnostics pass, each language server's start when a
pipeline finishes loading, and the build systems' pipeline addins as it
loads (meson and cmake ninja, cargo cargo), looked up their programs on
the main thread: in the pipeline's runtime with
ide_pipeline_contains_program_in_path(), then on the host. Each lookup
spawns `which` and waits for it, and in a podman runtime that is a
`podman exec`, 134-177 ms each. With a toolbox as the runtime, opening
a Python file froze the editor for 0.3-0.8 s.

_ide_pipeline_find_programs_async() makes the same lookups on a worker
thread, filling the runtimes' path caches. IdeDiagnosticTool runs it
before each pass, IdeLspService once per pipeline before it creates the
launcher, and the pipeline before it loads its addins, for ninja,
ninja-build and cargo. All of them then make their lookups on the main
thread as before, and find every answer cached.

Only the podman and host runtimes are looked up there: both answer from
an IdePathCache, which locks. Others stay on the main thread, as a
Flatpak runtime reaches the context's runtime manager for its SDK, which
is main-thread only; each lookup left to it is logged ("Leaving PROGRAM
in RUNTIME to the main thread").

The podman runtime, looked up from threads now:
- caches every answer but a cancelled wait and podman's 125 while
  `podman start` had not yet exited, which was cached as a miss for
  good; any other status (127 from a container without `which`, 125 from
  one that will not start) is a miss, cached, as before, so it costs one
  lookup per program rather than one per diagnostics pass;
- lets a worker thread wait until `podman start` has exited, whoever
  started it, under a condition, while the main thread never waits;
- frees its id, JSON object and path cache in finalize, not destroy,
  since a lookup on a worker may still use them.
- forgets its programs with gbp_podman_runtime_forget_programs(), on
  ide_path_cache_clear(), for a caller that changed what the container
  has installed; a lookup begun before that caches nothing, so an
  answer from before the change cannot come back.
